      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can\u0027t be 100% certain of this, but...\n\nWe\u0027ve previously sent announcements on this topic such as this one: https://docs.partner.android.com/partners/guides/gki/whatsnew#2023-dec-15\n\n... and we received no complaints. So we could send another announcement if needed.\n\nIMO, there aren\u0027t really any vendor hooks that would make use of this e.g. in `binder_alloc.c`. The `struct binder_alloc` internals are only exposed because the compiler needs the complete type to be defined under `struct binder_proc`. However, it is still exposed so there is always a chance that someone might use it behind the vendor hook.\n\nI\u0027ll double check how badly this is needed fist and we\u0027ll send an announcement before merging.",
